BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dallahan and If You Must Know
DTSTART:20261121T193000
DTEND:20261121T213000
DTSTAMP:20261121T180522Z
UID:927d6c01032c122ce905e18badaa3c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Next Stage Arts and Twilight Music present two of contemporary
  Celtic music’s most exciting voices—Dallahan and If You Must Know. Fe
 aturing fiddle\, guitar\, banjo\, accordion\, bagpipes\, harp\, and invent
 ive arrangements that push tradition forward while honoring its roots\, Da
 llahan and If You Must Know infuse high-energy traditional folk with bold 
 innovation. Forged in Scotland and Ireland’s traditional music scene whi
 le drawing on the music of the Balkans and North America\, Dallahan takes 
 listeners on a journey across styles and borders in a dazzling live show. 
 The band creates its own distinctive brand of world folk\, delivered with 
 stunning virtuosity. This performance is part of Next Stage’s Local & Gl
 obal Series\, made possible by a 2026 Music in Action grant from Live Musi
 c Society. Next Stage Arts\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/dallahan-a
 nd-if-you-must-know-20-10-2026-15-17-27
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equinox Documentary Film Festival
DTSTART:20261121T130000
DTEND:20261121T153000
DTSTAMP:20261121T180522Z
UID:8c516c72c12d3f754cd37a783ac9f1@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Equinox Documentary Film Festival\, now in its 7th year\, 3rd 
 at the Savoy Theater in Montpelier\, bringing together the best of documen
 tary shorts to a single-day\, 180 min screening in one of Vermont's most b
 eautiful theaters. With films from up-and-coming filmmakers through to sea
 soned professionals\, the Equinox Documentary Film Festival is an event wh
 ich showcases the best of locally driven social and environmental initiati
 ves.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Savoy Theater\, 26 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/equinox-do
 cumentary-film-festival-05-11-2026-13-53-06
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Art Saturday
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTSTAMP:20261121T180522Z
UID:50e81610b33284f6ceeceb582a1573@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an art-making activity inspired by current BCA Cen
 ter exhibitions and explore processes and materials used by the exhibiting
  artists. All ages are welcome. Youth must be accompanied by an adult. The
 re is a suggested program contribution of $10/per participant. All are wel
 come regardless of ability to pay. Please consider a contribution for adul
 ts who’d like to join in the art-making activity. Advanced registration 
 encouraged\; drop-ins welcome. Sign up here. Thank you to our BCA Educatio
 n Supporter\, Northfield Savings Bank. BCA’s fall exhibitions are suppor
 ted in part by the Maslow Family Foundation. Dark Botanica has support fro
 m Higher Ground Presents\, Red Wagon Plants\, and American Meadows. Hospit
 ality sponsors: Lake Champlain Chocolates\, City Market Onion River Co-Op
 \, and Sugarsnap Catering. Burlington City Arts is supported in part by th
 e Vermont Arts Council & the National Endowment for the Arts.\n\nSources: 
 Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Burlington City Arts Center\, 135 Church st
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/family-art
 -saturday-12-10-2026-12-18-40
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Folded Paper Ornaments with Beads Workshop at Fiddleheads Gallery
DTSTART:20261121T110000
DTEND:20261121T133000
DTSTAMP:20261121T180522Z
UID:908715f48daa794a318a43df36c58b@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Fold\, shape\, and create a beautiful German Bell ornament fro
 m a simple square of paper! With just 10 folds\, you’ll transform decora
 tive paper into a distinctive bell\, then personalize it with beads and a 
 coordinating tie-loop. There’s plenty of time to experiment with differe
 nt papers\, colors\, and embellishments as you create at least two unique 
 bells to take home. Come fold\, play\, and create! Age range: 15+\n\nSourc
 es: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fiddleheads Gallery\, Deerfield Valley Art Association\, 105 Main
  Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/folded-pap
 er-ornaments-with-beads-workshop-at-fiddleheads-gallery-17-11-2026-11-32-4
 6
END:VEVENT
