BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:KCP Presents: Upright Citizens Brigade All-Stars
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTSTAMP:20261121T180522Z
UID:e968016627c60836fee75bf9e5780e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:ST. JOHNSBURY – The KCP Presents Performing Arts Series welc
 omes fast and fearless improv comedy troupe Upright Citizens Brigade All-S
 tars\, to Fuller Hall\, St. Johnsbury\, on November 21st\, at 7pm. Student
 s accompanied by adults get free tickets! Anything can happen when the Upr
 ight Citizens Brigade All-Stars take the stage—and it usually does. Draw
 n from the legendary comedy company that launched countless stars of telev
 ision and film\, including Amy Poehler\, Kate McKinnon\, Aubrey Plaza\, Do
 nald Glover\, Aziz Ansari\, Bowen Yang\, Ilana Glazer\, Ed Helms\, Ego Nwo
 dim\, Zach Woods and many others\, UCB veterans have gone on to star in 
 “The Office\,” “Saturday Night Live\,” “Parks and Recreation\,
 ” “The Daily Show\,” and countless others. These master improvisers 
 create hilarious scenes\, unforgettable characters\, and unexpected storie
 s entirely on the spot\, inspired by audience suggestions. Smart\, fearles
 s\, and wildly inventive\, every performance is unique and unrepeatable. W
 hether you're a longtime fan of improv or simply love to laugh\, the UCB A
 ll-Stars deliver an evening of quick wit\, brilliant comic timing\, and no
 nstop surprises. The KCP Presents Performing Arts Series showcases world-c
 lass international touring acts throughout Vermont’s Northeast Kingdom. 
 Renowned for bringing big city entertainment to Vermont’s small towns\, 
 KCP Presents has scheduled ten shows this season\, including a joyful Sout
 h African youth choir\, enchanting Scandinavian folk music\, thrilling Jap
 anese drummers\, death-defying Chinese acrobats\, and live dance\, comedy
 \, and music acts from all over the United States. Season and single-show 
 tickets for KCP Presents 2026-27 shows are on sale now. Early bird discoun
 ts are available for single shows when purchased three weeks in advance. S
 tudent admission is free to St. Johnsbury Academy and Lyndon Institute per
 formances. To buy tickets or learn more\, visit www.catamountarts.org or w
 ww.kcppresents.org. Alternatively\, call 802-748-2600 or visit the Catamou
 nt Arts box office at 115 Eastern Avenue\, St. Johnsbury. The KCP Presents
  Series is produced by Catamount Arts working in association with Kingdom 
 County Productions and supported by generous local sponsors including Auto
 saver Group\, Community National Bank\, Lyndon Institute\, Northern Counti
 es Healthcare\, EastRise Credit Union\, NVRH\, Passumpsic Bank\, St. Johns
 bury Academy\, Seven Days\, The Point\, NHPR\, WYKR/Yankee Broadcasting\, 
 Green Mountain Broadcasters\, Vermont Public\, Downs Rachlin Martin\, Unio
 n Bank\, Moose River Lake and Lodge\, Kingdom Trails\, Triad Results\, Ant
 hony’s Diner\, Badger\, Peabody and Smith Realty\, and Seven Days\, with
  grant funding from the Vermont Arts Council.\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Ve
 rmont Public
LOCATION:Catamount Arts\, St. Johnsbury\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/kcp-presen
 ts-upright-citizens-brigade-all-stars-05-11-2026-17-39-02
END:VEVENT
